{"name":"Buenos Aires","hex":"#f4dcc1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Buenos Aires","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The capital city of Argentina.\n\n The Argentinian government.","The Argentinian government."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buenos Aires","blocks":[{"text":"Buenos Aires, officially the Autonomous City of Buenos Aires, is the capital and largest city of Argentina. It is located on the southwest of the Río de la Plata. Buenos Aires is classified as an Alpha− global city, according to the GaWC 2024 ranking. The city proper has a population of 3.1 million and its urban area has a population of 16.7 million, making it the 21st most populous metropolitan area in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Puerto_Madero%2C_Buenos_Aires_%2840689219792%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Puerto_Madero%2C_Buenos_Aires_%2840689219792%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires"},{"title":"LATAM Airlines Colombia","blocks":[{"text":"LATAM Airlines Colombia is a Colombian airline based in El Dorado International Airport in Bogotá. It is the second-largest air carrier in Colombia, after Avianca. It operates scheduled regional domestic passenger services, as well as a domestic cargo service. Its main hub is El Dorado International Airport in Bogotá."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LATAM_Airlines_Colombia"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Caminito%2C_La_Boca.jpg/500px-Caminito%2C_La_Boca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Caminito%2C_La_Boca.jpg/1280px-Caminito%2C_La_Boca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia